// Onboarding validation and latency — Lab 03
// Reusable checks for confirming a freshly onboarded device is streaming, and
// for measuring ingestion latency honestly. Replace the device filter as needed.
//
// TIMEZONE WARNING: DeviceEvents/DeviceInfo Timestamp renders in the portal's
// configured timezone. Latency computed against a local wall-clock reads wrong
// until converted. Use ingestion_time() when the question is "when did MDE
// RECEIVE this", not "when did it happen on the device". See Lab 03 §7.

// --- 1. Is the sensor streaming at all? ---
DeviceEvents
| where DeviceName startswith "lab-win11"      // adjust to your device
| where Timestamp > ago(1h)
| order by Timestamp asc
| take 20

// --- 2. Ingestion latency — event time vs. cloud-receive time ---
// A large, consistent gap here does NOT mean backfill; it usually means the
// portal timezone differs from the clock you are comparing against. A small
// gap (single-digit minutes) is a live, healthy stream.
DeviceEvents
| where DeviceName startswith "lab-win11"
| extend EventTime = Timestamp, IngestTime = ingestion_time()
| extend GapMinutes = datetime_diff('minute', IngestTime, EventTime)
| project EventTime, IngestTime, GapMinutes, ActionType
| order by EventTime asc
| take 15

// --- 3. Telemetry window summary — first/last event, first ingest, count ---
DeviceEvents
| where DeviceName startswith "lab-win11"
| summarize
    FirstEvent  = min(Timestamp),
    FirstIngest = min(ingestion_time()),
    LastEvent   = max(Timestamp),
    TotalEvents = count()

// --- 4. Onboarding status and connectivity type ---
// Confirms the connectivity choice (Standard vs Streamlined) actually applied,
// rather than trusting the download-time selection.
DeviceInfo
| where DeviceName startswith "lab-win11"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, OnboardingStatus, ConnectivityType
| order by Timestamp desc
| take 1

// --- 5. Attribution — which account ran a process ---
// The point of endpoint telemetry: actions tie to an identity and a lineage.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where DeviceName startswith "lab-win11"
| where Timestamp > ago(1h)
| where FileName =~ "powershell.exe"
| project Timestamp, FileName, ProcessCommandLine, AccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName
| order by Timestamp desc
